@obverse
1. a-na pu-šu-ke-en₆ qi₂-bi-ma
#tr.en.(o 2): Speak to Pušu-kēn, thus (says) Lamassī: 
2. um-ma la₂-ma-si₂-ma 9 TUG₂-HI.A
3. ku-lu-ma-a na-aš₂-a-kum
#tr.en.(o 7): Kullumā is bringing you nine textiles; Idi-Suen is bringing you three textiles; Ela refused to accept textiles (for transport); Idi-Suen refused to accept 5 textiles (for transport).
4. 3 TUG₂-HI.A i-di₂-su₂-en₆ na-aš₂-a-kum
5. e-la₂ TUG₂-HI.A la₂-qa₂-a-am la₂ i-mu-a
6. i-di₂-su₂-en₆ 5 TUG₂-HI.A la₂-qa₂-a-am
7. la₂ i-mu-a mi₃-šu ša ta-aš₂-ta-na-pa₂-ra-ni
8. um-ma a-ta-ma TUG₂-HI.A
#tr.en.(o 10): Why do you write me all the time as follows, "The textiles, which you use to send me, are not good."
9. ša tu₃-uš-te₂-ne₂-bi-li-ni
10. la₂ dam-qu₂ / ma-nu-um
@bottom
1. za-ak-ru-um
#tr.en.(r 4): Who is the fellow, who lives in your house, who is decrying the textiles, when they arrive before him? 
